# 🔍 Phishing Detector Frontend — Sanity Check Report

**Date:** 2026-03-01  
**Scope:** Production readiness & fast CORS review

---

## 🚨 CRITICAL: Issues That Will Break in Production

### 1. Hardcoded `localhost` API endpoint
**File:** [script.js](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detector-frontend/phishing-detector-frontend/script.js#L4)

```js
const response = await fetch("http://127.0.0.1:8003/predict", { ... });
```

- This will **fail immediately** in production — the browser will try to call `127.0.0.1:8003` on the user's own machine.
- This **also triggers a mixed-content block** if the frontend is served over HTTPS (browser refuses `http://` fetch from an `https://` page).

> [!CAUTION]
> **Fix:** Use a relative URL or environment-driven config:
> ```js
> const API_BASE = window.location.hostname === "localhost" || window.location.hostname === "127.0.0.1"
>   ? "http://127.0.0.1:8003"
>   : "https://your-production-api.example.com";
> ```

---

### 2. CORS whitelist is `localhost`-only (backend)
**File:** [main.py](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detection-api/phishing-detection-api/app/main.py#L15-L24)

```python
allow_origins=[
    "http://localhost:5500",
    "http://127.0.0.1:5500",
],
```

- The backend will **reject** requests from any production domain.
- "Fast CORS" = the browser sends a **preflight `OPTIONS`** request first; if the origin isn't whitelisted, the actual `POST` never fires.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Fix:** Add your production frontend origin:
> ```python
> allow_origins=[
>     "http://localhost:5500",
>     "http://127.0.0.1:5500",
>     "https://your-production-frontend.example.com",
> ],
> ```
> **Never** use `allow_origins=["*"]` with `allow_credentials=True` — browsers block that combo.

---

## ⚠️ HIGH: Issues That Degrade Experience

### 3. No `<meta name="viewport">` tag
**File:** [index.html](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detector-frontend/phishing-detector-frontend/index.html#L3-L6)

- Despite having responsive CSS breakpoints (`768px`, `480px`), **mobile browsers will render the page at desktop zoom** without:
  ```html
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  ```

### 4. Missing `<meta name="description">` (SEO)
- No meta description means search engines will auto-generate a snippet. For a public-facing tool this is a missed opportunity.

### 5. Validation error is never cleared
**File:** [script.js](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detector-frontend/phishing-detector-frontend/script.js#L34-L40)

- Once `validationError` is shown (empty URL), it stays even after the user types and clicks Analyze with a valid URL. The `click` handler only shows it but never hides it.

### 6. `Enter` key doesn't submit
- Users expect `Enter` to trigger analysis. Currently only the button click is wired up.

---

## 🟡 MEDIUM: Polish & Robustness

### 7. No URL format validation
- Any string is sent to the backend — including things like `hello` or `   `. At minimum a basic regex check avoids unnecessary API calls.

### 8. `result.className =` wipes all classes
**File:** [script.js](file:///c:/Users/USER/Desktop/Phishing_Detector/phishing-detector-frontend/phishing-detector-frontend/script.js#L49)

```js
result.className = analysis.isPhishing ? "phishing" : "safe";
```
- This nukes every class on `#result`, then re-adds via `classList.remove("hidden")` on the next line. It works *by accident* but is fragile — any future class added to `#result` will be silently dropped.

### 9. Right-panel carousel has no rotation logic
- Three `.info-block` elements exist with `position: absolute` and only the first has `.active`. There's no JS to rotate them, so two panels are permanently invisible.

### 10. Intel strip `#intelText` is always empty
```html
<span id="intelText"></span>
```
- No JS populates this. It renders as an empty strip with just the label "LIVE THREAT INTEL".

